  "description": "Fuaran.Core.Idl — the interface-definition engine: a typed model of a domain's node vocabulary (kinds, unions, enums, records, four-way optionality, a declarable node envelope, hosted slots) plus the legs generated from it — a schema-driven canonical encoder/decoder, an F# structural-layer emitter with a declared-support channel (docs, splices, host projections), a JSON-schema emitter, a stability diff classifier over two artifact revisions, and the codegen trust boundary (allowlisted `Custom` resolution, sanitisation). The engine only; a vocabulary is DATA a domain declares and owns in its own repo. FSharp.Core + Fuaran.Core.Wire only.",
